                {
                    "type": "definition",
                    "term": {
                        "text": "Swift tools"
                    },
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "label": "Current requirement",
                            "text": "Swift 6.2"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "These are the package's current declared floors. Firstlight does not promise support for earlier versions. Both the iOS and Android renderers are required for a public component; the same documented EDGE example works on both platforms."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "After changing NativePHP versions, run "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "composer update",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " and "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "php artisan native:install --force",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " so bundled PHP binaries, native project files, and plugin copies match the resolved release."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Mobile 4.7 supplies the validation and Android focused-input flush seams Firstlight uses; Mobile UI 0.9 requires Mobile 4.7. "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "ValidatesFields",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " extends upstream "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "ValidatesInput",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", and native and Firstlight fields share the current "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "FieldErrors",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " bag. Existing Firstlight screen code does not need a trait swap."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        "runtime-response-contract": {
            "title": "Runtime response contract",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "Supported response-revision contract"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Extend "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "FirstlightUI\\NativeComponent",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", not the upstream EDGE base, for screens using Firstlight controls, with NativePHP at the floors above."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The base stamps the "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "final chrome-wrapped root",
                            "strong": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " with the integer prop "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "firstlight_response_revision",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". Its counter is private, process-wide, and monotonically increasing across screen instances within the PHP process, not component state to bind, persist, or set yourself. An otherwise unchanged full response therefore differs from the previous frame and reaches the renderers. The one exception is the final frame "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "back()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " publishes before popping the screen: it keeps the current revision, so an unchanged screen is not republished mid-pop. On iOS such a frame would re-push the screen being left."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This deliberately bypasses whole-frame equality suppression for each completed screen response. It trades that deduplication saving for reliable reconciliation of unchanged values; publication cost still needs soak/performance qualification."
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Normal Blade paths are automatic: a global Laravel "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "View",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " returned from "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "render()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "$this->view()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", and the inferred view all receive the revision."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Programmatic Element roots must return "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "$this->response($element)",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " from "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "render()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". This adds normal screen chrome as well as the root revision. Use it only for raw Element content, not an already-completed "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "view()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " or "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "fromView()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " response. Custom "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "wrapWithChrome()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " overrides must call the parent."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "text": "Nested children are emitted untouched; partials are unstamped. Neither is an independent full response under this contract."
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "renderStreaming()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " is final and returns "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "false",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". Streaming bypasses this contract and cannot be opted into by a subclass."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Existing concerns such as "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "ValidatesFields",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " remain usable separately, but adding a trait to the upstream base does not provide this publication contract."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The revision is "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "not a per-event acknowledgement",
                            "strong": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". It does not prevent publication coalescing or serialize simultaneous proposals. Applications must not infer that every event receives a separately observable response. This is a screen-rendering contract, not a replacement for NativePHP's generic publisher: framework-owned loading placeholders and error/dump overlays are outside it."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "On navigation, the farewell response also closes Firstlight Bottom Sheets and Modals, including nested overlays, without changing the screen's bound visibility properties. Mobile's cleanup handles its own overlay types; Firstlight extends it to its namespaced types."
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "Upstream context and qualification"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The October 2026 Android and iOS PHP 8.5.11 bundles still suppress byte-identical frames in the shared C runtime. Android "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "treePublicationId",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", shipped in Mobile 4.1.0 ("
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "#280",
                            "link": 0
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "), only helps after a publication reaches Kotlin. The cross-platform bug "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "#365",
                            "link": 1
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " remains upstream; the response revision makes Firstlight independent of it."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mobile 4.7 additionally skips matching frame fingerprints in PHP. Firstlight keeps the response revision so repeated rejected values still publish distinct responses; the upstream optimisation is not a per-event acknowledgement."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The permanent implementation was checked on October 19, 2026 with Mobile 4.6.0, Mobile UI 0.8.0, and the official PHP 8.5.11 bundles: 14 nonstreaming phases each on an Android emulator and iOS simulator. Each phase delivered three proposals through a normal Blade screen using Firstlight's base, without app-authored revision props. Repeated Switch/Pill rejection, Segmented rejection, validation, accepted Switch changes, 500 ms rejection, and rapid same-control bursts passed. Rapid bursts deliberately coalesce a second tap while pending; they do not prove one response per physical tap. The earlier spike did not reproduce a baseline Segmented failure, so these results do not establish a Segmented fix."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Package regression tests cover Blade, inferred views, hand-built responses, remounts, nested children, and unstamped partials. Firstlight 1.0.0 was verified on physical iOS and Android devices. Soak/performance testing, including simultaneous controls, has not been recorded."
                }
            ]
        }
    },
